docs {
  MCP server. Run **MCP → Initialize** first: it opens a session and saves its id
  (`mcpSessionId`), which every other MCP request sends. Re-run it if a request answers
  "Missing session ID" or 404 (the server restarted).

  MCP requests use the static `LUMITRACE_MCP_AUTH_TOKEN` as a bearer token; it works in both
  `token` and `oauth` mode. Answers come as an event stream: the JSON-RPC reply is the
  `data:` line.
}
